---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base
    title="Privacy policy"
    description="How Paws & Whiskers handles what you tell us through this website: what we collect, why, who processes it, how long we keep it and how to ask us about it."
    breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }]}
>
    <Hero tone="paper" icon="shield" eyebrow="Privacy" heading="Your privacy, in plain words" lead="This site is small and tries to know as little about you as it can. Here is exactly what that means." />

    <div class="prose page">
        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>Only what you send us through the appointment form: your name, phone number and email address, your pet’s name, species and age, the reason for the visit and the times that suit you. We use it to arrange the appointment and to keep your pet’s record.</p>
        <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
        <p>This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics or advertising scripts, and loads nothing from other companies’ servers: the fonts and photographs are served from this site. Our web server keeps short-lived logs of requests (addresses and pages) to keep the site secure, and deletes them after 14 days.</p>
        <h2>Who handles it</h2>
        <p>Form submissions go straight to our practice system, which our team uses to manage appointments and records. We do not sell, rent or share your details with anyone for marketing, ever.</p>
        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>Appointment requests that do not lead to a visit are deleted after 12 months. Clinical records are kept for as long as the law requires veterinary records to be kept.</p>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete what we hold about you. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.business.email}`}>{site.business.email}</a> or call <a href={`tel:${site.business.phoneE164}`}>{site.business.phone}</a>, and we will reply within a month.</p>
        <p class="muted">This is an example privacy notice for a fictional practice. A real practice should have it checked against the laws where it operates.</p>
    </div>
</Base>

<style>
    .page {
        padding: var(--space-8) 0 var(--section);
        font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
</style>
